<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis José de Orbegoso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis José de Orbegoso was a Peruvian general and president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1833. Facing rebellion, he invited the Bolivian president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a> into Peru in 1835, which led to the creation of the Peru-Bolivian Confederation. He became president of its North Peruvian Republic but broke with Santa Cruz in 1838.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-jose-de-orbegoso.jpg" alt="Luis José de Orbegoso" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Probably José Gil de Castro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Orbegoso1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
